IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ll81-nouns`

-- Row il-81. THE REFERENCES, as typed values: the four items I1 to I4 of the Land Law, 5729-1969 ("the Law"), the pages that print the words each item cites, the pages that print the target, and the instructions of I4.
-- Tests of the controls are in ll81-tests-controls.l4, and the four assertions that FAIL on purpose (one per item) are in ll81-tests-red.l4.
--
-- THE QUOTATION LINES.
-- `src:N` lines are expanded mechanically from the excerpt of the Hebrew Wikisource consolidation, revision 2962167 (UNOFFICIAL, so CONSOLIDATION-ONLY), by tools/srcquote.py; N is the line number in the whole page, which the excerpt's header lists.
-- `ext:[tag]` lines quote the Hebrew read from a deposited page image (registers/source-bundle/pages/): the tag names the instrument (sh = Sefer HaChukim, nh18 = Dinei Medinat Yisrael, Nusach Chadash 18) and the printed page. They are official instruments. Footnote numbers and quotation marks the pages print around an inserted text are left out of the quoted lines.
-- A line marked CONSOLIDATION-ONLY rests on the consolidation alone and on no page image.
-- Nothing is quoted from memory. Every date, number and section below is on a quotation line or in NOTES.md.
-- A date typed as `the issue date its footer prints` is the date of the issue, and it is never a day of effect.
-- The typed Hebrew strings follow the code points of the consolidation (the gershayim sign, the maqaf and the en dash); the pages print a double quote, a hyphen or a long dash in those places. NOTES.md says what was compared and what was not.

§ `References`

